+### `GET /orders/export`
+
+Every order as CSV (`text/csv; charset=utf-8`, CRLF line ends); `GET /orders/export.csv` serves the
+same.
+
+The header row `id,customer,total,status,created_at` comes first, then one row per order,
+ascending by the `order` query — `created` (the default), `total` or `customer`; any other value
+sorts by `created`; ties by `id`. With no orders, the body is the header row alone. A field holding
+a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted, its quotes doubled; text that starts with `=`, `+`, `-`,
+`@`, a tab or a carriage return gets a leading `'`. The export reads `exportBatchSize` orders at a
+time (Configuration).
+
